WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.473
Welcome to Tiny Siege.

00:00:01.473 --> 00:00:05.490
You and a friend build fortresses and choose secret orders.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:12.587
Your mission is simple: destroy the opponent's crown marked command room while keeping your own standing.

00:00:12.587 --> 00:00:17.723
Choose Build, select a piece, then click empty cells on your fortress.

00:00:17.723 --> 00:00:20.951
You can place up to three pieces per round.

00:00:20.951 --> 00:00:23.886
Click a planned piece again to undo it.

00:00:23.886 --> 00:00:27.555
Every piece needs a connected path to the ground.

00:00:27.555 --> 00:00:28.846
Expecting a shot?

00:00:28.846 --> 00:00:35.378
Choose Reinforce and select up to three friendly blocks, including your command room.

00:00:35.378 --> 00:00:41.530
Each costs two supplies, repairs six health, and shields four damage this round.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.416
Defenses happen before incoming fire.

00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:46.940
Choose Fire and aim at the enemy.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.847
Cannon hits the first block in a row.

00:00:49.847 --> 00:00:51.835
Drill hits the first two.

00:00:51.835 --> 00:00:53.900
Scatter damages a cluster.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.648
Mortar drops on the exact cell, bypassing cover.

00:00:57.648 --> 00:01:03.843
Highlights preview the current targets, but new enemy walls can change the shot.

00:01:03.843 --> 00:01:08.841
Blocks without a connected path to the ground collapse after damage.

00:01:08.841 --> 00:01:12.515
Braces also connect diagonally, saving overhangs.

00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:18.468
Powder is cheap protection, but explodes into its four neighbors when destroyed.

00:01:18.468 --> 00:01:21.335
Falling rubble causes no extra damage.

00:01:21.335 --> 00:01:24.394
Choose one action, then lock your order.

00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:27.147
You can also hold to save supplies.

00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:30.665
Both attacks resolve together after defenses.

00:01:30.665 --> 00:01:35.790
If both command rooms fall in the same round, the match is a draw.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.767
In local play, look away during your friend's turn.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:43.357
To play on separate devices, open Play online.

00:01:43.357 --> 00:01:46.089
Enter your name and create a room.

00:01:46.089 --> 00:01:48.898
Copy the invitation to your friend.

00:01:48.898 --> 00:01:52.176
They open it, enter their name, and join.

00:01:52.176 --> 00:01:55.298
Both players plan on their own screens.

00:01:55.298 --> 00:01:59.513
The server keeps orders secret until both are locked.

00:01:59.513 --> 00:02:03.305
Start with ten supplies and earn four each round.

00:02:03.305 --> 00:02:07.019
Mints earn extra income; arsenals boost damage.

00:02:07.019 --> 00:02:13.364
Rising pressure eventually damages both command rooms, so no siege lasts forever.

00:02:13.364 --> 00:02:20.097
Online, both players choose Next round to continue, or Settle the score for a rematch.

00:02:20.097 --> 00:02:21.799
Good luck, commander.

